{
  "id": "p4-w27-m4",
  "title": "HNSW is a skip list whose levels are graphs",
  "alt": "A hand-drawn whiteboard with three stacked layers of a navigable small-world graph: a top layer holding 0.39 percent of nodes joined by three long hops, a middle layer with 6.25 percent, and a bottom layer containing every node, with dotted drop lines showing the same node exists in every layer below and a numbered six-step red search path descending greedily to the query cross. Beside it a crossed-out k-d tree square is annotated that in 768 dimensions it visits 94 percent of nodes, an inset shows the two heaps of the inner loop as the week-14 Dijkstra frontier, an IVF panel rings three of seven k-means centroids as nprobe equals three, and three bars compare ef_search 40 at recall 0.95 and 980 QPS against ef_search 10 and brute force.",
  "width": 1000,
  "height": 852,
  "tier": "T2",
